2\\pi ),$  traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(4,5)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(h+a,k).$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(-2,5),$ $a=6$ and $b=4.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +5,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399531 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b497d42e-bb82-5ad8-b534-e2c147e1ff42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=36\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399533} {:answer/id #uuid "0713f8eb-12ff-5fe2-9526-65877bb581ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399534} {:answer/id #uuid "3969d63a-a2eb-506f-beb7-6cde82a0d05c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399535} {:answer/id #uuid "9a825ff3-cad9-54b1-8ffe-6c0d2f47c301" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399536} {:answer/id #uuid "da3c9fdb-6c6a-55f0-8a89-dc38f3583e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da3c9fdb-6c6a-55f0-8