os}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(-4,-4),$ $a=4$ and $b=6.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -4,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42d6d789-9a13-55ed-9aa3-a6599922e6d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=25\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404004} {:answer/id #uuid "ae0179db-bc3d-59ac-a7ab-f6e35d77cdda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404005} {:answer/id #uuid "22551caa-d93a-5d26-a64b-1d4d526c0551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404006} {:answer/id #uuid "61661834-8abe-5e9e-95ce-3916c77f8307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404007} {:answer/id #uuid "10b69a37-8e76-5d45-bf03-9dcbeccb702d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae0179db-bc3d-59ac-a7ab-f6e35d77cdda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404005} :answer-field/id #uuid "6729ae77-9d58-5d6c-9396-7d1f8b6ef681" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404003}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9082f86b-7c0f-5dd7-b074-5c0e7d067128" :question/math-academy-id "q-79287" :question/problem "![](images/07/07ec13485a828c8f5cd99ae2fbc3f7444135ba3c1cdf790762edb01b9726317e.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate the ellipse shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(3,2),$ $a=3$ and $b=5.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0a50ab1-4ada-57e2-8605-70a502bab6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404011} {:answer/id #uuid "32f648c8-3d4d-551c-a0fe-e98c1f6d2eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404012} {:answer/id #uuid "89052cbe-3422-56ea-9b9a-942801acf80e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404013} {:answer/id #uuid "8b13ccd7-add3-5ba4-bf95-5440c51f18c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404014} {:answer/id #uuid "1c440c18-9297-5a46-a77e-a81bd6a4fec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1,\\,y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0a50ab1-4ada-57e2-8605-70a502bab6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404011} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d9041eb-bfd0-524e-8602-d57198b3ea25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404010}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7a6a1e67-ac65-5715-8684-1ea8d5d95e68" :question/math-academy-id "q-79292" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7d45616d089e8f5d078ff48c949b26d0920074ab4b611ec71b491a0e18fd293c.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at $(3,1)$ with horizontal radius $1$ and vertical radius $2,$ as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(4,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(h+a,k).$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(3,1),$ $a=1$ and $b=2.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "The Parametric Equations of an Ellipse Centered at a General Point"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152190 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151992 :question/id #uuid "9abded65-4a6e-5ebc-b496-d61b28179288" :question/math-academy-id "e-6818" :question/problem "The semi-ellipse below is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx = 5\\cos\\theta, \\qquad y = 4\\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta?$\n\n![](images/6c/6ca367eb7dc7cbd8205cbd85ad6d2503f957defd3f9a10e7b510759f41e0c778.png)" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx= a\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=b\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in [0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=5$ and $b=4.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx= 5\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=4\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in [0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a semi-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta$ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the ellipse and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/a6/a64898381b2cf50c71a79a3dbcf02b9a83f320b8c2d1ba542b3beecc05e17625.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta$ to $\\left[0, \\pi\\right],$ we get the semi-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the semi-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx= 5\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=4\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in\\left[0, \\pi\\right].\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b51a7bc-7701-539f-9e20-dfc7f2574559" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "493b8640-4fdd-5d60-946f-939751c8af46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345977} {:answer/id #uuid "b84f1666-210b-572b-9813-7c6c6f7b754f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346954} {:answer/id #uuid "d511cf0c-a77c-5137-a47d-1d8bab162656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347224} {:answer/id #uuid "dc209651-386a-5003-b530-70073c38acc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answ