trict $\\theta $ to $[\\frac{3\\pi }{2},2\\pi ]$, we get the quarter-ellipse in the **fourth quadrant** (where $x\\ge 0$ and $y\\le 0$).\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the quarter-ellipse are \n\n$$\np=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,q=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [\\frac{3\\pi }{2},2\\pi ].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302359 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171799d9-7223-5dd4-a228-48e8aba86de5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "171799d9-7223-5dd4-a228-48e8aba86de5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300055} :answer-field/id #uuid "75df719e-462a-58a0-914e-a2e113fe9c32" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301591} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fff4831-cbfc-507b-91dd-e522a76e056b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fff4831-cbfc-507b-91dd-e522a76e056b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300378} :answer-field/id #uuid "f22e3862-a382-517b-a5d7-3aa3aed51c26" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301998}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b6c5d2b-dddb-56bf-8b0f-4abc2119254d" :question/math-academy-id "q-327835" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6f983fda4328227558e46aaaec454db2ccc0611331495c923ad1d90c7cb3df8a.png)\n\nThe semi-ellipse above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$ Assume $\\theta $ is between $0$ and $2\\pi .$\n\n$\\theta \\in [${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$]$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=8$ and $b=3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a semi-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the ellipse and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/10/101d9b26027bc5667009b0c7af69fa190c987c362122402fce62daec5833092f.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\pi ]$, we get the semi-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the semi-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca6398a1-b09b-5fe5-8b22-062bcee1ef3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca6398a1-b09b-5fe5-8b22-062bcee1ef3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300971} :answer-field/id #uuid "62bfcebf-053f-576b-a004-657c68248546" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301544} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "140964c7-df0e-5db6-94ce-6a0240be4dfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "140964c7-df0e-5db6-94ce-6a0240be4dfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300040} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6439ef2-f460-56da-9ba7-f298fa601bbf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301914}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c61885c3-83e2-5a8d-b365-c4d1e934aa7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-327847" :question/problem "![](images/ab/ab9ef90cf863fee6776667a967d5939ba3564564d5d7626e07aaa868baea6a87.png)\n\nThe quarter-ellipse above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$ Assume $\\theta $ is between $0$ and $2\\pi .$\n\n$\\theta \\in [${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$]$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(-2,1),$ with $a=4$ and $b=5.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-ellipse, we again interpret $\\theta $ as the central angle measured from the horizontal line through the center $(h,k).$ On the quarter-arc where both $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\ge 0$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\ge 0$ (moving from the rightmost point to the topmost point), the parameter must satisfy $\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\n![](images/df/df6c12657a6a487f93ec3a6213be8ea16e68d363001bdf0ddb8ff68b5201a8c4.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$, we get the quarter-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the quarter-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eecdf539-f4c9-5e2a-b1d3-147515693798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eecdf539-f4c9-5e2a-b1d3-147515693798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301145} :answer-field/id #uuid "908f284e-1908-5bfa-9308-7074a7ede550" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301687} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc4981ef-e57a-51b9-b310-d03c74ee1689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc4981ef-e57a-51b9-b310-d03c74ee1689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301053} :answer-field/id #uuid "e34a02c9-d0c9-59ab-b604-48db38e67691" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301945}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2e29b9a7-ba3d-59be-8f85-186fc6a70498" :question/math-academy-id "q-328327" :question/problem "![](images/52/5234672d8176a0a04bbc3feecfe13092ff116a25682ae055286f1fe858b8a754.png)\n\nThe half-ellipse above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$ Assume $\\theta $ is between $0$ and $2\\pi .$\n\n$\\theta \\in [${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$]$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(-1,2),$ $a=5,$ and $b=3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a half-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the ellipse and the horizontal line through its center.\n\n![](images/1b/1b2d7617af37197dfd2702b4497263e563458b0bf11c622308220def93b688a9.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}],$ we get the half-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the half-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a9f41de-144e-5379-8d7e-1e17fed1cc44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345584} {:answer/id #uuid "60811d34-2531-5a15-97a2-b323f7a440ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346186} {:answer/id #uuid "636af2c9-f212-547b-ae0a-6bee08eb660c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,2\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346216} {:answer/id #uuid "c53b6a3c-e3e4-57a8-b745-a6cea4f29a87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347059} {:answer/id #uuid "c883c73e-dd77-569e-a6ca-c43b10cb3266" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60811d34-2531-5a15-97a2-b323f7a440ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ]" 